Sh:[{label:"CompScience",url:"https://www.compscience.com"}],Mg:[RE,SE],modules:[{type:"hero",content:{date:"Jan 7, 2025",headline:"CompScience improves industrial worksite safety with on-demand image and video analysis",ps:"CompScience uses Gemini 2.5 Pro and 2.5 Flash to analyze worksite footage and mitigate realtime hazards. Through their Safe Work Plan, Safety Pulse, and Safety Search products, they scale expert knowledge to help workers stay safe on the job.",authors:[{name:"Dan Walton",role:"Principal Engineer, CompScience"},
{name:"Vishal Dharmadhikari",role:"Product Solutions Engineer"}],thumbnail:{src:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/compScience/CompScience_hero.jpg",type:"image",alt:"CompScience showcase hero"}}},{type:"stats",content:{stats:[{value:"400%",description:"Adoption of Safe Work Plan vs. standard techniques"},{value:"15K+",description:"Hours of video footage processed"},{value:"60",description:"Detailed risk reports deployed to industry"}]}},{type:"cta",content:{link:"https://aistudio.google.com/prompts/new_chat?model=gemini-flash-latest"}},
{type:"text",content:{body:"\n            <p>\n              CompScience is on a mission to eliminate workplace accidents by using AI to provide Safe Work Plans, real-time alerts, and comprehensive safety reports derived from worksite video footage. Partnering with professional risk experts like the National Safety Council, CompScience serves over 100 industrial customers across a variety of sectors, helping them identify risks before they become injuries.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              The core challenge for CompScience is the sheer volume of data. Industrial worksites generate hundreds of hours of video every day. Manually reviewing this footage for potential hazards is impossible at scale. To turn this massive unstructured dataset into concise, actionable safety information, CompScience turned to the Gemini API.\n            </p>"}},
{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Scaling expert safety knowledge with Gemini 2.5 Pro</h2>"},body:"\n            <p>\n              CompScience utilizes Gemini 2.5 Pro to build their Safe Work Plan application. When maintenance workers encounter unplanned work in a factory, they can use their cellphones to take photos of the situation.\n            </p>"}},{type:"images",content:{items:[{image:{src:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/compScience/CompScience_inline_01.jpg",alt:"Phone screen allowing users to input job details to conduct a quick Risk Prediction."},
legend:"Workers can submit photos from job sites to generate a Safe Work Plan detailing hazards and proposed safeguards."}]}},{type:"text",content:{body:"\n            <p>\n              2.5 Pro processes these images, reasons through complex safety assessment rubrics, and provides expert-informed advice and guidance. These recommendations can then be saved as standard safe company procedures, effectively digitizing and scaling expert safety knowledge.\n            </p>"}},{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Processing over 15 thousand hours of video with Gemini 2.5 Flash</h2>"},
body:"\n            <p>\n              Beyond static images, CompScience needs to process continuous video streams for their Safety Pulse and Safety Search products. They utilize Gemini 2.5 Flash to periodically assess worksite cameras for immediate issues and to rapidly search through hundreds of hours of archived video in minutes to generate impact reports.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              According to Daniel Walton, Principal Engineer at CompScience, 2.5 Flash\u2019s native video processing capabilities are a key differentiator, noting that \u201cvideo processing just isn\u2019t available\u201d at the same level with other AI providers they tested. To manage the high throughput of video data, CompScience leverages the Files API, using multiple threads to upload video and generate insights efficiently.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              A recent development for CompScience is utilizing Gemini 2.5 Flash\u2019s ability to generate bounding boxes around identified hazards within continuous video or images. This visual grounding allows them to help identify unsafe behaviors or conditions in their reports, a feature Walton notes is \u201conly possible with Gemini 2.5 Flash\u201d for their specific use case.\n            </p>"}},
{type:"images",content:{items:[{image:{src:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/compScience/CompScience_inline_02.jpg",alt:'Two screenshots of the CompScience SafetyPulse interface. The left screen shows a video feed from a construction site with a green bounding box around a crane, alongside an "Alert" log identifying a suspended load hazard. A "Take Action" pop-up menu allows users to select corrective measures. The right screen displays a "Safety Overview" dashboard with camera activity thumbnails, alert summaries, and a generated report listing potential safety hazards and recommendations for improvement.'},
legend:"Gemini 2.5 Flash processes job site security photos for safety managers to review, then generates actionable daily reports."}]}},{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Proactively improving safety and mitigating hazards</h2>"},body:"\n            <p>\n              By integrating Gemini models, CompScience currently delivers video-driven safety reports to hundreds of customers. The effectiveness of their AI-driven approach has led the National Safety Council to include the CompScience Safe Work Plan system for their own members, scaling these safety benefits to a broader industrial audience.\n            </p>"}},
{type:"related_cases",content:{zi:["pascalai","ava","raindrop"]}}]},{title:"Forio",Vh:"Learn how incoming MBA students use Veo to generate professional-grade video for their business simulations.",slug:"forio",Xi:"https://aistudio.google.com/apps/bundled/veo_studio?showPreview=true&showAssistant=true",thumbnail:{url:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/forio/forio_thumb.jpg",alt:"Forio showcase preview"},Sh:[{label:"Forio",url:"https://forio.com"}],Mg:[VEb],modules:[{type:"hero",content:{date:"DEC 19, 2025",
headline:"Enabling creative expression in Wharton\u2019s MBA program with Veo",authors:[{name:"Drew Marx",role:"Forio"},{name:"Alisa Fortin",role:"Product Manager"},{name:"Vishal Dharmadhikari",role:"Product Solutions Engineer"}],thumbnail:{src:"https://www.gstatic.com/aistudio/case_studies/Forio_hero.jpg",type:"image",alt:"Forio showcase hero"}}},{type:"cta",content:{link:"https://aistudio.google.com/apps/bundled/veo_studio?showPreview=true&showAssistant=true"}},{type:"text",content:{body:'\n            <p>\n              <a href="http://forio.com">Forio</a> is a leading simulation company building experiential learning solutions for higher education and enterprise, with over 10 million learners having used their platform since 2001. One of their flagship deployments is for The Wharton School of the University of Pennsylvania, specifically for Management 6100, a required first-week course where student teams run an electric car company, navigating leadership challenges and making core business decisions.\n              <br>\n              <br>\n              For the 2025 major revision of this simulation, Wharton and Forio sought to incorporate AI capabilities to balance analytical decision-making with creative expression. Forio integrated <a href="https://aistudio.google.com/apps/bundled/veo_studio?showPreview=true&showAssistant=true">Veo</a> directly into their Epicenter web-based simulation platform, enabling 150 teams of six students to complete marketing projects using generative AI.\n            </p>'}},
{type:"images",content:{items:[{image:{src:"https://ai.google.dev/static/showcase/forio/images/forio_inline_01.jpg",alt:"Forio inline image 1"}}]}},{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Scaling creativity for 850 MBA students</h2>"},body:"\n            <p>\n              Previously, creative expression within business simulations was largely limited to text, numbers, and static images. Video content was unfeasible due to the need for animation skills, expensive tools, and weeks of post-production time\u2014none of which fit within the tight constraints of a one-week intensive program. By using Veo, students could generate professional-grade video clips for their car company commercials using only natural language prompts.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              Forio\u2019s implementation in Epicenter was designed for high concurrency and low latency, as it needed to handle over 850 students dispersed across Wharton\u2019s Huntsman Hall, often working in simultaneous waves. The platform successfully handled three waves of students, managing 50 concurrent video generations at a time.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              On average, Veo 2 generated these eight-second clips in approximately 45 seconds, allowing teams to iterate rapidly on their creative concepts during live simulation sessions. Over the course of the week, Wharton MBA students generated between 1,300 and 1,500 video clips.\n            </p>"}},
{type:"text",content:{header:{headline:"<h2>Hands-on experience, more engaging curriculum</h2>"},body:"\n            <p>\n              The introduction of Veo generated exceptional enthusiasm. Faculty reported that engagement was so high that students frequently ran late to subsequent sessions because they did not want to stop creating. The activity was noted as a dramatic improvement over previous exercises with similar learning goals.\n            </p>"}},{type:"images",content:{items:[{image:{src:"https://ai.google.dev/static/showcase/forio/images/forio_inline_02.jpg",
alt:"Forio inline image 2"}}]}},{type:"text",content:{body:'\n            <p>\n              Wharton is the leading voice regarding AI in business, leading the way regarding AI research as well as usage of AI within their classrooms. Course faculty include Nancy Rothbard, Adam Grant, Samir Nurmohamed, and Michael Parke.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              By integrating Veo, Wharton and Forio demonstrated that generative AI can effectively power creative expression in traditionally analytical business education, providing students with hands-on experience with tools they will likely encounter in their future careers.\n            </p>\n            <p>\n              To start building with Veo, read our <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs">API documentation</a>.\n            </p>\n            '}},
