 to the shot. Show detailed texture: a glossy sheen, a satisfying snap, a molten center.\nSound Design Cues: The video should be generated with the following audio in mind: a rich, satisfying "snap" or "crack" of chocolate, a subtle "gasp" of delight from the characters, and a sweeping, uplifting orchestral score that swells during the transitions.\n4. Scene-by-Scene Breakdown:\n(Scene 1: The Origin - 2 seconds)\nSetting: A dense, misty Mesoamerican jungle. Sunlight streams through the canopy, illuminating a stone temple ruin.\nAction: An ancient Mayan priestess, adorned with jade and intricate tattoos, grinds cacao beans on a stone metate.\nCamera: Slow dolly in on her face. Her eyes, initially serious and then eye shut\nTRANSITION: As her eyes shut, MATCH CUT to...\n(Scene 2: The Royal Indulgence - 3 seconds)\nSetting: A lavish, candle-lit Baroque salon in 17th century Paris. Opulent gold leaf, velvet curtains, and the soft hum of a harpsichord.\nAction: A French aristocrat in a powdered wig and silk gown delicately holds a tiny porcelain cup. A servant pours a thick, steaming hot chocolate.\nCamera: Close-up on her face.\nTRANSITION: As her eyes shut, MATCH CUT to...\n(Scene 3: The Future Relic - 3 seconds)\nSetting: A sleek, minimalist apartment in a futuristic Tokyo-style megacity, 2099. Outside the panoramic window, holographic advertisements and flying vehicles stream by in the neon-drenched night.\nAction: A woman in a simple, silver jumpsuit holds a small, perfectly geometric cube. She explains to her android companion that it\'s "real, ancient chocolate," a rare artifact. She places it on her tongue. The cube instantly melts.\nCamera: Extreme close-up on her mouth and eyes. A single, happy tear rolls down her cheek as she tastes a flavor she\'s only read about. Her eyes close in nostalgic bliss for a time she never knew.\nTRANSITION: As her eyes shut, we don\'t match cut, but instead begin a RAPID MONTAGE.',
